      "extract": "Remarkable measurements from the collisions of large nuclei, Au + Au at the Relativistic Heavy Ion Collider (RHIC) and Pb + Pb at the Large Hadron Collider (LHC), show that O(104) particles yield signs of collective behavior in the form of, e.g., near- perfect fluidity [1–3], strangeness enhancement [4, 5], quarkonium suppression [6–8], and, in particular, the en- ergy loss of high-momentum particles [9–11],",
      "extractCut": true
    },
