        }
      ],
      "extract": "The standard candle of final-state partonic energy loss in high-energy hadronic collisions is the nuclear modification factor, Rh AB(pT ) = 1 Ncoll dN h AB/dpT dN h pp/dpT , (1) where dN h AB/dpT and dN h pp/dpT are the pT -differential numbers of hadrons h produced in A + B and p + p col- lisions, respectively, and Ncoll is the number of binary collisions, typically computed by experiments using the Glauber model",
      "extractCut": true
    },
